
=== Sayari MCP -- 20 tools, full inputSchema ===

--- get_entity_profile ---
Get the full profile of a Sayari entity including all attributes (names, addresses, identifiers, status, financials), relationships (shareholders, directors, officers, subsidiaries, trade partners), and risk factors (sanctions, PEP, Basel AML index, CPI score). Requires a Sayari entity_id. Use after resolving or searching for an entity. Treat the profile as evidence, not infallible ground truth: confirm that names, identifiers, countries, entity type, and relationships all fit the same legal entity. If the node appears conflated or carries critical risk flags, explain the ambiguity instead of silently normalizing it.
{
  "properties": {
    "entity_id": {
      "title": "Entity Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "relationships_limit": {
      "default": 50,
      "title": "Relationships Limit",
      "type": "integer"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "entity_id"
  ],
  "title": "get_entity_profileArguments",
  "type": "object"
}

--- get_entity_summary ---
Get a condensed profile of a Sayari entity with attributes and risk factors but WITHOUT relationships. Faster and cheaper than get_entity_profile. Use when you only need to check an entity's basic info, risk status, or identifiers without exploring its network. Treat the summary as evidence, not infallible ground truth: confirm that names, identifiers, countries, and entity type all fit the same legal entity before relying on it.
{
  "properties": {
    "entity_id": {
      "title": "Entity Id",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "entity_id"
  ],
  "title": "get_entity_summaryArguments",
  "type": "object"
}

--- lookup_risk_factors ---
Look up Sayari risk factor definitions, categories, and scoring methodology. Use this when you encounter risk flags (e.g. basel_aml_index, cpi_score, forced_labor_index, regulatory_action) in entity profiles, search results, or traversal outputs and need to understand what they mean, how they are scored, or how to interpret their levels. Broad lookups stay compact; filter by specific risk factor IDs when you need the richest available scoring detail. Call this early in an investigation to understand the risk landscape before interpreting results.
{
  "properties": {
    "ids": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Ids"
    }
  },
  "title": "lookup_risk_factorsArguments",
  "type": "object"
}

--- lookup_ontology ---
Look up Sayari reference data by category: entity types, relationship types, countries, identifiers, attributes, currencies, languages, regions, enums, or source types. Use when you need to understand valid values for API filters, interpret enum fields in results, or explain data model concepts to the user.
{
  "$defs": {
    "OntologyCategory": {
      "enum": [
        "entity_types",
        "relationships",
        "countries",
        "identifiers",
        "attributes",
        "currencies",
        "languages",
        "regions",
        "enums",
        "source_types"
      ],
      "title": "OntologyCategory",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "category": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/OntologyCategory"
    },
    "ids": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Ids"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "category"
  ],
  "title": "lookup_ontologyArguments",
  "type": "object"
}

