}

--- get_record ---
Retrieve the original source record from Sayari's database. Use when the user wants to verify the source of a specific data point, needs a document URL for evidence, or asks 'where does this information come from?'. Requires a record_id, which appears in entity profiles and traversal results.
{
  "properties": {
    "record_id": {
      "title": "Record Id",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "record_id"
  ],
  "title": "get_recordArguments",
  "type": "object"
}

--- search_entities ---
Search Sayari's knowledge graph for entities matching a query string. Use for broad or investigative searches where you have partial information, want to explore multiple potential matches, or need to filter by entity type, country, or risk factors. Treat candidate selection as a same legal entity question, not same-name matching: compare identifiers, countries, source quality, relationships, and risk flags before choosing a record. If results look conflated across jurisdictions or entity types, surface the ambiguity instead of guessing. Supports elasticsearch simple query string syntax. Uses the shared response_mode contract. `response_mode=auto` is the default, uses the smaller AUTO_RESPONSE_SIZE working budget, and may ignore strict `limit` semantics to fill the response budget for the agent. Leave `response_mode` unset unless you have a clear reason to override it. Do not force `response_mode=full` on broad search/list tools just because it exists; use `full` only when the working set is already very small or the user explicitly asks for richer detail. If the question is still broad, do aggregate analysis with the facet tools first instead of forcing `full` on a row-returning tool. Read `items` as the working set, use row `next_action` for drill-down, inspect `quality_flags` for ambiguity or data gaps, and use structured `continue` only when you truly need more breadth. In `full`, `_guidance` contains only `selection_rule`, `ambiguity_rule`, and `verification_rule`.
{
  "$defs": {
    "ResponseMode": {
      "description": "Supported response modes for heavy read tools.",
      "enum": [
        "auto",
        "full",
        "compact",
        "export"
      ],
      "title": "ResponseMode",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "query": {
      "title": "Query",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "limit": {
      "default": 25,
      "title": "Limit",
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "offset": {
      "default": 0,
      "title": "Offset",
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "response_mode": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/ResponseMode",
      "default": "auto"
    },
    "page_token": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Page Token"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "query"
  ],
  "title": "search_entitiesArguments",
  "type": "object"
}

--- search_entity_facets ---
Return entity search facet counts for aggregate analysis without spending the response budget on result rows. Use this when you need to understand the shape of a broad entity query before drilling into specific records. This tool is best for comparing countries, entity types, and other facet buckets across the search results at an aggregate level; then use those buckets to rewrite a narrower `search_entities` query or move directly to the relevant entity tool once you know what slice of the result set matters.
{
  "properties": {
    "query": {
      "title": "Query",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "bucket_limit": {
      "default": 10,
      "title": "Bucket Limit",
      "type": "integer"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "query"
  ],
  "title": "search_entity_facetsArguments",
  "type": "object"
}

